Using LLM Summarization in Your Scikit-Learn Pipelines with Scikit-LLM Learn how to build an architecture that blends Scikit-LLM estimators for text summarization with traditional scikit-learn methods into a single, unified pipeline for summarizing and classifying raw, messy text. By Iván Palomares Carrascosa , KDnuggets Technical Content Specialist on November 3, 2026 in Language Models Introduction Using traditional, lightweight machine learning classifiers on text frequently requires condensing lengthy, often noisy raw text into clean signals to succeed. Therefore, it wouldn't be crazy to think of using a large language model (LLM) for text summarization as a preprocessing stage before feeding cleaner texts to the downstream classification model. What if we could do this seamlessly as part of a traditional, scikit-learn-based pipeline where LLM-driven summarization can coexist with traditional data preprocessing, training, and inference? And what if we could do all of this using exclusively free tools? Look no further. In this article, we will learn how to build an architecture that blends Scikit-LLM estimators for text summarization with traditional scikit-learn methods into a single, unified pipeline for summarizing and classifying raw, messy text, bringing together the best of both worlds: LLMs and classical machine learning models. Integrating LLM-Driven Summarization in a Machine Learning Pipeline This example can be run entirely in a Google Colab notebook. It uses Groq 's LLM API to fully rely on free models. A prerequisite is to access the Groq website , register, and generate your own API key. Once it's generated, carefully copy your API key (it is shown only once) and paste it as a new "Secret" variable in Google Colab, found at the key icon on the left-hand side of Colab. Name the secret variable GROQ_API_KEY . After that, we start our notebook by installing Scikit-LLM: !pip install scikit-llm -q Now, into the Python code. The first step is to configure the environment surrounding Scikit-LLM, routing our requests through Groq's API instead of the default OpenAI API. This will help us leverage Groq's free, friendly, and efficient pre-trained models, bypassing per-token costs. from google.colab import userdata from skllm.config import SKLLMConfig # Retrieving API key and routing to Groq's free-tier OpenAI-compatible endpoint groq_key = userdata.get('GROQ_API_KEY') SKLLMConfig.set_gpt_url("https://api.groq.com/openai/v1") SKLLMConfig.set_openai_key(groq_key) Next, we define the "training" data . It consists of a small set of initial documents along with their corresponding labels. The documents are intentionally lengthy, somewhat noisy, and verbose, just like in many real-world scenarios. Without a prior summarization to extract relevant signals from the text, directly obtaining numerical, machine learning-friendly representations from these texts would inevitably propagate the noise: # Raw, lengthy documents and their corresponding class labels X_long_texts = [ "The new solar panel technology efficiency has increased by 15% due to the novel perovskite layer, significantly lowering the barrier to entry for residential use and driving green energy adoption by making installations cheaper and faster than ever before.", "Financial markets saw a sharp downturn today following the central bank's unexpected interest rate hike, leading to massive sell-offs in the tech sector and triggering volatility indices to reach their highest points in over three years.", "The clinical trial for the new arthritis medication showed promising results, reducing joint swelling by 40% in the control group without severe side effects, awaiting FDA approval which could bring relief to millions suffering from autoimmune disorders." ] y_labels = ["Energy", "Finance", "Healthcare"] Similar to few-shot classification, we only need a small, representative set of training examples to let the LLM we will load later know how to reason. No actual training of the LLM takes place. The next step is arguably the most critical: we are defining our three-step pipeline for machine learning-driven classification preceded by LLM-driven summarization , thereby integrating Scikit-LLM capabilities to accommodate specific tasks on pre-trained LLMs into a broader machine learning pipeline. The code below uses a GPTSummarizer object to encapsulate a compatible Groq model for summarization, namely openai/gpt-oss-20b . It then embeds the summarization step into the scikit-learn pipeline, followed by term frequency-inverse document frequency (TF-IDF) to obtain text representations of summarized texts rather than the original, lengthy ones. Finally, it defines and trains a logistic regression classifier using the label set defined before. from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression from skllm.models.gpt.text2text.summarization import GPTSummarizer # THREE-STEP MACHINE LEARNING PIPELINE FOR TEXT CLASSIFICATION, PRECEDED BY SUMMARIZATION # 1. Summarizer: Condenses long documents using the compatible model on Groq # 2. Vectorizer: Converts the concise summaries into numerical TF-IDF vectors # 3. Classifier: Learns to classify the TF-IDF vectors using standard Logistic Regression text_pipeline = Pipeline([ ('summarizer', GPTSummarizer( model="custom_url::openai/gpt-oss-20b", max_words=20 )), ('vectorizer', TfidfVectorizer()), ('classifier', LogisticRegression()) ]) # Fitting the entire pipeline end-to-end text_pipeline.fit(X_long_texts, y_labels) You might be wondering why just three training instances in X_long_texts could be enough to train the last-stage logistic regression classifier. It's not because the classifier has truly learned the broad concepts of 'Energy', 'Finance', and 'Healthcare'. Instead, it succeeds due to two pipeline mechanics working in tandem: the LLM first acts as a precise filter that condenses noisy text into "canonical" keywords. After that, the downstream vectorizer naturally limits its whole vocabulary to those few remaining words, turning the classification task into a pretty easy, largely trivial keyword-matching game. Next, we take a look at the summaries produced for the three training examples to verify they make sense: # Inspecting the summaries of "training" examples, accessing the 'summarizer' object train_summaries = text_pipeline.named_steps['summarizer'].transform(X_long_texts) print("--- TRAINING DATA SUMMARIES ---") for label, original, summary in zip(y_labels, X_long_texts, train_summaries): print(f"[{label.upper()}]
Original: {original}
Summary: {summary}
") Output: --- TRAINING DATA SUMMARIES --- [ENERGY] Original: The new solar panel technology efficiency has increased by 15% due to the novel perovskite layer, significantly lowering the barrier to entry for residential use and driving green energy adoption... Summary: New perovskite solar panels boost efficiency by 15%, reducing costs and accelerating residential green energy adoption. [FINANCE] Original: Financial markets saw a sharp downturn today following the central bank's unexpected interest rate hike, leading to massive sell-offs in the tech sector and triggering volatility indices... Summary: Markets plunged after unexpected rate hike, causing tech sell‑offs and high volatility. [HEALTHCARE] Original: The clinical trial for the new arthritis medication showed promising results, reducing joint swelling by 40% in the control group without severe side effects, awaiting FDA approval... Summary: New arthritis drug trial reduces swelling by 40% with no severe side effects, pending FDA approval.

閒魚智慧監控系統 [中文] ｜ English 基於 Playwright 和 AI 的閒魚多工即時監控，提供完整的 Web 管理介面。 核心特性 Web 視覺化管理 : 任務管理、賬號管理、AI 標準編輯、執行日誌、結果瀏覽 AI 驅動 : 自然語言建立任務，多模態模型深度分析商品 多工併發 : 獨立配置關鍵詞、價格、篩選條件和 AI Prompt 高階篩選 : 包郵、新發布時間範圍、省/市/區三級區域篩選 即時通知 : 支援 ntfy.sh、企業微信、Bark、Telegram、Webhook等多渠道 定時排程 : 支援 Cron 配置週期性任務 賬號與代理輪換 : 多賬號管理、任務綁定賬號、代理池輪換與失敗重試 Docker 部署 : 一鍵容器化部署 截圖 🐳 Docker 部署（推薦） git clone https://github.com/Usagi-org/ai-goofish-monitor && cd ai-goofish-monitor
cp .env.example .env
vim .env # 填寫相關配置項 docker compose up -d
docker compose logs -f app
docker compose down 如果映象無法訪問或下載速度慢，可嘗試使用加速： docker pull ghcr.nju.edu.cn/usagi-org/ai-goofish:latest
docker tag ghcr.nju.edu.cn/usagi-org/ai-goofish:latest ghcr.io/usagi-org/ai-goofish:latest
docker compose up -d 預設 Web UI 地址： http://127.0.0.1:8000 Docker 映象已內建 Chromium，無需宿主機額外安裝瀏覽器。 官方映象地址： ghcr.io/usagi-org/ai-goofish:latest 更新映象： docker compose pull && docker compose up -d 如果你修改了 .env 中的 SERVER_PORT ，請同步更新 docker-compose.yaml 裡的埠對映。 docker-compose.yaml 預設會把 SQLite 主庫掛載到 ./data:/app/data ，資料庫檔案預設為 data/app.sqlite3 目前預設持久化這些目錄： data/ SQLite 主儲存（任務、結果、價格歷史） state/ 登入狀態 cookie 檔案 prompts/ 任務提示詞 logs/ 執行日誌 images/ 商品圖片與任務臨時圖片目錄 config.json 、 jsonl/ 、 price_history/ 首次升級到 SQLite 時用於相容匯入的舊資料來源 資料儲存與遷移 當前線上主儲存為 SQLite，預設路徑 data/app.sqlite3 可通過環境變數 APP_DATABASE_FILE 自定義資料庫路徑；Docker 預設設定為 /app/data/app.sqlite3 應用啟動時會自動建庫建表，並嘗試從舊的 config.json 、 jsonl/ 、 price_history/ 匯入一次歷史資料 state/ 、 prompts/ 、 logs/ 、 images/ 仍然是檔案系統目錄，不在 SQLite 中 商品圖片會臨時落到 images/task_images_<task_name>/ ，任務結束後預設會清理 首次升級完成並確認 data/app.sqlite3 中資料正確後，可視部署方式決定是否繼續保留舊的 config.json 、 jsonl/ 、 price_history/ 掛載 最少配置 變數 說明 必填 OPENAI_API_KEY AI 模型 API Key 是 OPENAI_BASE_URL OpenAI 相容介面地址 是 OPENAI_MODEL_NAME 支援圖片輸入的模型名稱 是 WEB_USERNAME / WEB_PASSWORD Web UI 登入賬號密碼，預設 admin/admin123 否 其餘配置見下方“配置說明”。 第一次使用 開啟預設 Web UI http://127.0.0.1:8000 並登入。 進入“閒魚賬號管理”，使用 Chrome 擴展 匯出並貼上閒魚登入態 JSON。 登入態檔案會儲存到 state/ 目錄，例如 state/acc_1.json 。 回到“任務管理”，建立任務並綁定賬號後即可執行。 建立第一個任務 AI判斷 ：填寫“詳細需求”，提交後會彈出獨立進度彈窗，後臺非同步生成分析標準。 關鍵詞判斷 ：填寫關鍵詞規則，任務會直接建立，不經過 AI 生成流程。 區域篩選 ：已改為省 / 市 / 區三級選擇器，資料基於閒魚頁面抓取快照內建。 使用者使用說明 點選展開 Web UI 功能說明 任務管理 支援 AI 建立、關鍵詞規則、價格範圍、新發布範圍、區域篩選、賬號綁定、定時規則。 AI 任務建立是後臺 job 流程，提交後會開啟單獨的進度彈窗。 區域篩選會顯著縮小結果集，預設留空。 賬號管理 支援匯入、更新、刪除閒魚賬號登入態。 每個任務可指定賬號，也可不綁定並交給系統自動選擇。 結果檢視與執行日誌 結果頁和匯出功能現在從 SQLite 查詢，不再直接掃描 jsonl 檔案。 日誌頁按任務展示執行過程，便於排查登入態失效、風控和 AI 呼叫問題。 系統設定 可檢視系統狀態、編輯 Prompt、調整代理與輪換相關配置。 開發者開發 環境要求 Python 3.10+ Node.js + npm（本地驗證 Node v20.18.3 可完成前端構建） Playwright CLI 與 Chromium，首次執行前建議執行 python3 -m pip install playwright && python3 -m playwright install chromium Chrome / Edge 瀏覽器（Linux 環境也可使用 Chromium； start.sh 會先檢查瀏覽器是否存在） git clone https://github.com/Usagi-org/ai-goofish-monitor cd ai-goofish-monitor
cp .env.example .env 一鍵啟動 chmod +x start.sh
./start.sh start.sh 會先檢查 Playwright CLI 和瀏覽器前置條件；在前置條件滿足後自動安裝專案依賴、構建前端、複製構建產物並啟動後端。 手動啟動 # 後端 python -m src.app # 或 uvicorn src.app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000 --reload # 前端 cd web-ui
npm install
npm run dev FastAPI 啟動時會自動初始化 SQLite，並在首次啟動時嘗試匯入舊的 config.json/jsonl/price_history spider_v2.py 預設從 SQLite 讀取任務；只有顯式傳入 --config <path> 時才會走 JSON 配置相容模式 預設資料庫路徑為 data/app.sqlite3 Vite 開發伺服器會將 /api 、 /auth 、 /ws 代理到 http://127.0.0.1:8000 。 npm run build 先生成 web-ui/dist/ ， start.sh 再複製到倉庫根目錄 dist/ 。 FastAPI 負責提供根目錄 dist/index.html 和 dist/assets/ 。 ./start.sh 預設輸出訪問地址 http://localhost:8000 和 API 文件 http://localhost:8000/docs 。 測試與校驗 PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 pytest cd web-ui && npm run build 任務建立 API 點選展開 API 行為說明 POST /api/tasks/generate decision_mode=ai ：返回 202 和 job ，需要繼續輪詢進度。 decision_mode=keyword ：直接返回已建立任務。 GET /api/tasks/generate-jobs/{job_id} ：查詢 AI 任務生成進度。 POST /auth/status ：校驗 Web UI 登入憑據。 配置說明 點選展開常用配置項 AI 與執行時 OPENAI_API_KEY / OPENAI_BASE_URL / OPENAI_MODEL_NAME ：AI 模型接入必填項。 PROXY_URL ：為 AI 請求單獨指定 HTTP/SOCKS5 代理。 RUN_HEADLESS ：是否以無頭模式執行爬蟲；Docker 中應保持 true 。 SERVER_PORT ：後端監聽埠，預設 8000 。 LOGIN_IS_EDGE ：本地環境可切換為 Edge 核心；Docker 映象未內建 Edge，容器內會固定使用 Chromium。 PCURL_TO_MOBILE ：是否將 PC 商品連結轉換為移動端連結。 通知 NTFY_TOPIC_URL GOTIFY_URL / GOTIFY_TOKEN BARK_URL WX_BOT_URL TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN / TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID / TELEGRAM_API_BASE_URL WEBHOOK_* 代理輪換與失敗保護 PROXY_ROTATION_ENABLED PROXY_ROTATION_MODE PROXY_POOL PROXY_ROTATION_RETRY_LIMIT PROXY_BLACKLIST_TTL TASK_FAILURE_THRESHOLD TASK_FAILURE_PAUSE_SECONDS TASK_FAILURE_GUARD_PATH 完整示例見 .env.example 。 Web 介面認證 點選展開認證說明 Web UI 當前使用登入頁收集賬號密碼，並通過 POST /auth/status 校驗。 登入成功後，前端會在瀏覽器本地儲存登入狀態，用於路由守衛和 WebSocket 初始化。 預設賬號密碼為 admin/admin123 ，生產環境請務必修改。 🚀 工作流程 下圖描述了單個監控任務從啟動到完成的核心處理邏輯。主服務運行於 src.app ，按使用者操作或定時排程啟動一個或多個任務程序。 graph TD
    A[啟動監控任務] --> B[選擇賬號/代理配置];
    B --> C[任務: 搜尋商品];
    C --> D{發現新商品?};
    D -- 是 --> E[抓取商品詳情 & 賣家資訊];
    E --> F[下載商品圖片];
    F --> G[呼叫AI進行分析];
    G --> H{AI是否推薦?};
    H -- 是 --> I[傳送通知];
    H -- 否 --> J[儲存記錄到 SQLite];
    I --> J;
    D -- 否 --> K[翻頁/等待];
    K --> C;
    J --> C;
    C --> L{觸發風控/異常?};
    L -- 是 --> M[賬號/代理輪換並重試];
    M --> C; Loading 常見問題 點選展開常見問題 AI 任務建立為什麼不是立即完成？ AI 模式會先生成分析標準，再建立任務。現在該流程已改為後臺 job，提交後會顯示獨立進度彈窗，避免表單長時間卡住。 區域篩選為什麼預設建議留空？ 區域篩選會顯著減少搜尋結果，適合明確只看某個區域的場景。若你先驗證整體市場，建議先不填。 本地頁面開啟後提示前端構建產物不存在？ 說明根目錄 dist/ 缺失。可直接執行 ./start.sh ，或先在 web-ui/ 裡執行 npm run build ，再確認構建產物已複製到倉庫根目錄。 ./start.sh 為什麼提示缺少 Playwright 或瀏覽器？ 這是指令碼的前置檢查。請先安裝 Playwright CLI 與 Chromium，並確保系統中可用 Chrome / Edge（Linux 環境也可用 Chromium），然後重新執行 ./start.sh 。 致謝 點選展開致謝內容 本專案在開發過程中參考了以下優秀專案，特此感謝： superboyyy/xianyu_spider 以及感謝LinuxDo相關人員的指令碼貢獻 @jooooody 以及感謝 LinuxDo 社群。 以及感謝 ClaudeCode/Gemini/Codex 等模型工具，解放雙手 體驗Vibe Coding的快樂。 注意事項 點選展開注意事項詳情 請遵守閒魚的使用者協議和robots.txt規則，不要進行過於頻繁的請求，以免對伺服器造成負擔或導致賬號被限制。 本專案僅供學習和技術研究使用，請勿用於非法用途。 本專案採用 MIT 許可證 釋出，按"現狀"提供，不提供任何形式的擔保。 專案作者及貢獻者不對因使用本軟體而導致的任何直接、間接、附帶或特殊的損害或損失承擔責任。 如需瞭解更多詳細資訊，請檢視 免責宣告 檔案。 Star History

GitHub Copilot CLI The power of GitHub Copilot, now in your terminal. GitHub Copilot CLI brings AI-powered coding assistance directly to your command line, enabling you to build, debug, and understand code through natural language conversations. Powered by the same agentic harness as GitHub's Copilot coding agent, it provides intelligent assistance while staying deeply integrated with your GitHub workflow. See our official documentation for more information. 🚀 Introduction and Overview We're bringing the power of GitHub Copilot coding agent directly to your terminal. With GitHub Copilot CLI, you can work locally and synchronously with an AI agent that understands your code and GitHub context. Terminal-native development: Work with Copilot coding agent directly in your command line — no context switching required. GitHub integration out of the box: Access your repositories, issues, and pull requests using natural language, all authenticated with your existing GitHub account. Agentic capabilities: Build, edit, debug, and refactor code with an AI collaborator that can plan and execute complex tasks. MCP-powered extensibility: Take advantage of the fact that the coding agent ships with GitHub's MCP server by default and supports custom MCP servers to extend capabilities. Full control: Preview every action before execution — nothing happens without your explicit approval. We're still early in our journey, but with your feedback, we're rapidly iterating to make the GitHub Copilot CLI the best possible companion in your terminal. 📦 Getting Started Supported Platforms Linux macOS Windows Prerequisites (On Windows) PowerShell v6 or higher An active Copilot subscription . See Copilot plans . If you have access to GitHub Copilot via your organization or enterprise, you cannot use GitHub Copilot CLI if your organization owner or enterprise administrator has disabled it in the organization or enterprise settings. See Managing policies and features for GitHub Copilot in your organization for more information. Installation Install with the install script (macOS and Linux): curl -fsSL https://gh.io/copilot-install | bash Or wget -qO- https://gh.io/copilot-install | bash Use | sudo bash to run as root and install to /usr/local/bin . Set PREFIX to install to $PREFIX/bin/ directory. Defaults to /usr/local when run as root or $HOME/.local when run as a non-root user. Set VERSION to install a specific version. Defaults to the latest version. For example, to install version v0.0.369 to a custom directory: curl -fsSL https://gh.io/copilot-install | VERSION= " v0.0.369 " PREFIX= " $HOME /custom " bash Install with Homebrew (macOS and Linux): brew install copilot-cli brew install copilot-cli@prerelease Install with WinGet (Windows): winget install GitHub.Copilot winget install GitHub.Copilot.Prerelease Install with npm (macOS, Linux, and Windows): npm install -g @github/copilot npm install -g @github/copilot@prerelease Launching the CLI copilot On first launch, you'll be greeted with our adorable animated banner! If you'd like to see this banner again, launch copilot with the --banner flag. If you're not currently logged in to GitHub, you'll be prompted to use the /login slash command. Enter this command and follow the on-screen instructions to authenticate. Authenticate with a Personal Access Token (PAT) You can also authenticate using a fine-grained PAT with the "Copilot Requests" permission enabled. Visit https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new Under "Permissions," click "add permissions" and select "Copilot Requests" Generate your token Add the token to your environment via the environment variable GH_TOKEN or GITHUB_TOKEN (in order of precedence) Using the CLI Launch copilot in a folder that contains code you want to work with. By default, copilot utilizes Claude Sonnet 4.5. Run the /model slash command to choose from other available models, including Claude Sonnet 4 and GPT-5. Container image The Copilot CLI is also available as a container image that runs the CLI as a headless server for Copilot SDK clients. Images are published to ghcr.io/github/copilot-cli for linux/amd64 and linux/arm64 . This image is for connecting SDK clients to a server, not for interactive terminal use. Set a connection token and a GitHub token, then start the server: export COPILOT_CONNECTION_TOKEN= " $( openssl rand -hex 32 ) " docker run --rm \
  -p 127.0.0.1:4321:4321 \
  -e COPILOT_CONNECTION_TOKEN \
  -e COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN \
  ghcr.io/github/copilot-cli:latest Set COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN in your environment before running the command. For version-pinned deployments, use a release tag instead of latest . See the container image guide for SDK connection examples, configuration, security considerations, and build instructions. Experimental Mode Experimental mode enables access to new features that are still in development. You can activate experimental mode by: Launching with the --experimental flag: copilot --experimental Using the /experimental slash command from within the CLI Once activated, the setting is persisted in your config, so the --experimental flag is no longer needed on subsequent launches. Experimental Features Autopilot mode: Autopilot is a new mode (press Shift+Tab to cycle through modes), which encourages the agent to continue working until a task is completed. Each time you submit a prompt to GitHub Copilot CLI, your monthly quota of premium requests is reduced by one. For information about premium requests, see About premium requests . For more information about how to use the GitHub Copilot CLI, see our official documentation . 🔧 Configuring LSP Servers GitHub Copilot CLI supports Language Server Protocol (LSP) for enhanced code intelligence. This feature provides intelligent code features like go-to-definition, hover information, and diagnostics. Installing Language Servers Copilot CLI does not bundle LSP servers. You need to install them separately. For example, to set up TypeScript support: npm install -g typescript-language-server For other languages, install the corresponding LSP server and configure it following the same pattern shown below. Configuring LSP Servers LSP servers are configured through a dedicated LSP configuration file. You can configure LSP servers at the user level or repository level: User-level configuration (applies to all projects):
Edit ~/.copilot/lsp-config.json Repository-level configuration (applies to specific project):
Create .github/lsp.json in your repository root Example configuration: { "lspServers" : { "typescript" : { "command" : " typescript-language-server " , "args" : [ " --stdio " ], "fileExtensions" : { ".ts" : " typescript " , ".tsx" : " typescript " }
    }
  }
} Viewing LSP Server Status Check configured LSP servers using the /lsp command in an interactive session, or view your configuration files directly. For more information, see the changelog . 📢 Feedback and Participation We're excited to have you join us early in the Copilot CLI journey. We're building quickly. Expect frequent updates--please keep your client up to date for the latest features and fixes! Your insights are invaluable! Open an issue in this repo, join Discussions, and run /feedback from the CLI to submit a confidential feedback survey!
